 "id": "T16B-h8pin",
 "title": "Knuckle sleeve running fit on its pin (bronze bush bore vs m6 dowel)",
 "mode": "linear",
 "units": "mm diametral clearance (< 0 = the knuckle is pressed onto its pin)",
 "requirement": "Each knuckle turns on its pin, so the sleeve bore is never smaller than the pin.",
 "notes": "A sintered bronze bush comes F7 (3.006-3.016) and closes to H7 (3.000-3.010) when pressed into a rigid H7 housing; a printed PA6-CF knuckle closes it somewhere in between, so the bore is taken as uniform over 3.000-3.016. The m6 dowel is 3.002-3.008. The lower limit stays 0.000 (line-to-line is accepted: oil-impregnated bush, H7/h6-type sliding fit [A], worst case only, and the assembly check turns every pair by hand). The rev B pins are graded to the pressed bore so each pair is 0.000-0.020 (case revb: pin_clear 0.020), which T16 needs.",
